# Tooling clones (Vibe-Trading MCP server lives outside the app tree)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP config -- machine-specific, and a live auto-launch path
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.mcp.json` at a project root is auto-discovered by MCP-aware tooling, which
# launches the declared command as a process with no sandbox. The server it
# points at (Vibe-Trading) registers order-placement tools, on the same machine
# that holds the brokerage ledger. It is also machine-specific by construction
# -- `tools/write_mcp_config.py` exists to regenerate it locally, and its own
# docstring says so -- and committing it leaked an absolute path containing a
# developer's username. Generate it per machine; never track it.
.mcp.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UAT sandbox -- disposable, rebuildable, and large
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `uat/sandbox/` holds the isolated ledger a persona run trades into plus a copy
# of the daily bar store (~19MB). Both are rebuildable: the ledger from the run's
# own `imports/*.csv`, the bars from `data/store/bars`. The run *artifacts* under
# `uat/runs/` are committed on purpose -- they are synthetic, they carry no
# personal financial data, and they are what the enhancement loop reads.
uat/sandbox/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session scratch -- working files, never a deliverable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.scratch/` is where a session drops one-off probe scripts, coverage dumps and
# per-card working directories while it is figuring something out (~50 directories,
# ~3MB at the time of writing). None of it is input to anything: the cards that
# matter are in `backend/app/paper/library/`, the rounds that matter are in
# `strategy-program/rounds/`, and a probe script that proved a point has already
# served its purpose by the time the finding is written down. Committing it would
# add hundreds of files that no later reader can tell apart from real library
# content.
.scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paper desk local state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/paperdesk/inception.json` is the desk's inception-date override -- a
# per-machine display setting a person sets in the UI, in the same category as
# `data/accounts.toml` above: it describes *this* checkout's session, not the
# programme. Tracking it would mean one developer's chosen window silently
# re-running every agent's trades on someone else's clone, and it is precisely
# the persisted-state-plus-render-crash combination that took the Paper Desk page
# down once already.
data/paperdesk/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini review packets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Throwaway working files produced by `tools/gemini_review_bundle.py` for pasting
# into the Gemini web app / Antigravity. Regenerated on demand; never input.
.gemini-review/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only documents — quote the real ledger, never tracked
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `docs/local/` holds documents that quote the owner's real ledger in enough
# detail that they cannot be tracked: per-lot dollar figures, sale dates, ACAT
# control numbers, Roth contribution dates. HANDOFF.md and MIGRATION.md's full
# text live here, along with any report whose numbers turned out to be the
# owner's own money rather than backtest or institutional data. They stay
# readable on this machine, because the engineering history they carry is
# worth keeping -- a tracked stub at each original path says where the rest
# went and why. Never track this directory; a single `git add -A` here would
# put the real ledger's own numbers straight into history.
docs/local/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Persona vault -- dated personal notes on named influencers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/vault/` is the Obsidian vault the persona agents read and write
# (`Settings.vault_dir`): one dated note per YouTube video, filed under the
# influencer it came from. It was untracked but nothing above ignored it, so a
# `git add -A` would have committed every note in it -- the same failure mode
# the `data/rawData/` incident described at the top of this file, just in a
# directory that incident never touched. Ignore it explicitly rather than
# trust that it stays unstaged by luck.
data/vault/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Korean translation cache
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/i18n_cache/` holds `ko.json`, the on-display Korean translation cache
# for the i18n system. It is rebuildable from the English source strings and
# is machine-local -- the same category as the derived stores and caches
# below -- it just lives under `data/` because the i18n system put it there
# first rather than under `data/cache/`.
data/i18n_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Round 33 run logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/round33/*.log` are console logs from the dynamic-universe round's loop
# and bake-off runs -- the same category of reproducible working state as
# `data/loop/*` above: not part of the programme's record, just the output of
# a run that already wrote its findings elsewhere.
data/round33/*.log

# Backfill task packets (tools/backfill_task_bundler.py) -- throwaway hand-off staging.
.backfill-tasks/

# Backfill replies (the pasted-back external-agent output for those packets) and the retry log the
# scheduled task appends to. Neither is part of the record: a reply is re-ingestable from the
# packet, and the log is yt-dlp/transcript-API console noise. Both were unignored until the
# 2026-09-07 security audit found them one `git add -A` away from the remote.
.backfill-replies/
data/backfill_retry.log
